{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00153 - MONDO_1567",
  "verbalization": "Ergocalciferol is associated with Nephrocalcinosis through a chain of indications that involve hypercalcemia and calcium compounds. The drug is linked to Hypercalcemia Disease, which is a key driver of Nephrocalcinosis, as indicated by the presence of calcium lactate gluconate and calcium gluconate in the pathway. These calcium-based compounds are known to contribute to kidney stone formation and calcium deposition, which are central mechanisms underlying Nephrocalcinosis. The evidence suggests that Ergocalciferol may exacerbate hypercalcemia, thereby increasing the risk of calcium-related kidney damage. While the exact mechanism of action remains unclear, the shared pathway highlights a potential role of calcium metabolism in the development of Nephrocalcinosis, with Ergocalciferol acting as a mediator in this process. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of hypercalcemia and calcium metabolism in the pathogenesis of Nephrocalcinosis, positioning Ergocalciferol as a potential contributor to this condition.",
